+## When beforeSession throws
+
+- `beforeSession` runs inside the orchestrator's `try` block, so a thrown `Error` fires `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting at the caller with that same error, on both `processMessageStream` and `processMessage` ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession and still rejects when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L9)).
+- Nothing past `beforeSession` runs on that path — neither `beforeUserInput`, `afterUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, the provider, nor `afterModelResponse` — and `beforeSession` itself did not complete, so `afterSession` cannot assume setup finished and must guard against releasing a resource `beforeSession` never allocated ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession and still rejects when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L9)).
+
